# Access Control Patterns

## Bulk Permission Checking

### BulkPermissionChecker Usage
- Use [BulkPermissionChecker.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/access_control/contract_staffing/BulkPermissionChecker.java) for efficient bulk operations
- Supports multiple entity types: timesheets, candidates, jobs
- Optimizes data loading and permission checks

### Controller Pattern for Bulk Access Control
```java
@Validated
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/v1/access-control")
public class AccessControlController {
    
    @PostMapping("/bulk-check")
    public ResponseEntity<?> bulkCheck(@Validated @RequestBody BulkPermissionCheckRequest request) {
        BulkPermissionCheckResult result = accessControlChecker.allowsBulk(request);
        return apiResponder.respond(result, "Bulk permission check completed");
    }
}
```

### Request DTO Structure
```java
public record BulkTestRequest(List<Integer> entityIds) {
    public BulkTestRequest {
        if (entityIds == null || entityIds.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Entity IDs list cannot be null or empty");
        }
    }
}
```

### Service Layer Pattern
```java
@Service
public class AccessControlService {
    
    public BulkPermissionCheckResult checkBulkPermissions(List<Integer> entityIds) {
        List<BulkPermissionCheckRequest.BulkPermissionCheckItem> items = entityIds.stream()
            .map((entityId) -> {
                PermissionCheckContext permissionContext = new PermissionCheckContext();
                permissionContext.setPermission(Permission.VIEW_TIMESHEET);
                permissionContext.setPermissionLevel(PermissionLevel.YES);
                
                AccessControlCheckMetadataContext metadataContext = new AccessControlCheckMetadataContext();
                metadataContext.setTimesheetId(entityId);
                
                return BulkPermissionCheckRequest.BulkPermissionCheckItem.builder()
                    .entity(Entity.TIMESHEET)
                    .permissionCheckContext(permissionContext)
                    .accessControlCheckMetadataContext(metadataContext)
                    .build();
            })
            .toList();
            
        BulkPermissionCheckRequest request = BulkPermissionCheckRequest.builder().items(items).build();
        return accessControlChecker.allowsBulk(request);
    }
}
```

## Individual Permission Checking

### AccessControlChecker Usage
- Use [AccessControlChecker.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/access_control/contract_staffing/AccessControlChecker.java) for single entity checks
- Automatically loads required candidate and job data
- Performs permission validation with context

### Permission Context Pattern
```java
PermissionCheckContext permissionContext = PermissionCheckContext.builder()
    .permission(Permission.VIEW_TIMESHEET)
    .permissionLevel(PermissionLevel.YES)
    .build();

AccessControlCheckMetadataContext metadataContext = AccessControlCheckMetadataContext.builder()
    .timesheetId(timesheetId)
    .build();

accessControlChecker.allows(Entity.TIMESHEET, permissionContext, metadataContext);
```

## Available Permissions
- `VIEW_TIMESHEET`: Read access to timesheet data
- `EDIT_TIMESHEET`: Modify timesheet data
- `DELETE_TIMESHEET`: Remove timesheet data
- `APPROVE_TIMESHEET`: Approve timesheet submissions

## Available Entities
- `Entity.TIMESHEET`: Timesheet-related operations
- `Entity.CANDIDATE`: Candidate-related operations
- `Entity.JOB`: Job-related operations

## Response Handling
- Use [APIResponder.java](mdc:src/main/java/io/recruitcrm/microservice/timesheet/responses/APIResponder.java) for consistent response formatting
- Handle access denied exceptions via `GlobalExceptionHandler`
- Return structured responses with success/error status

